Slug: mcp-kit-3-premise
Type: question
Status: done
Owner: mcp-starter-template
Title: Does Claude Code actually reject draft-07 tool schemas?
Definition: browser-tab-mcp ran draft-07 servers fine on CC 2.1.300 -p; the 3.0 premise came from eqstack and was never reproduced here. Decides whether consumers must migrate or can just strip the $schema label.
Created: 2026-10-15T04:43:09Z
Updated: 2026-10-15T04:51:55Z
Repo: mcp-cli-starter-template
BlockedOn: eqstack
Asks: Paste the verbatim client error, CC version and surface, and a failing schema
Answer: eqstack, 2026-10-15 15:48 (bus xiGNE4FHl3B0): the error is real, verbatim from George's paste 2026-10-07 09:54Z:
+ "Error: Tool 'resolve_conversation' has an invalid outputSchema: JSON Schema declares an unsupported dialect ("$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"). The default validator supports JSON Schema 2020-12 only; pass a pre-configured Ajv instance to AjvJs"
+ Server imsg-mcp 1.25.5 (before the #184 strip). Surface and version unknown; the string ships in CC 2.1.300 and Claude Desktop 2.37337.1, Desktop is the likely surface. Does NOT reproduce with claude -p on 2.1.300 (draft-07 input+output schemas with structuredContent passed). PICK: strip $schema now, kit 3 on each consumer's own schedule; an Ajv2020 strict compile (kit 3 /testing) is the guard.
AnsweredBy: eqstack
Evidence: answered by eqstack
Ended: 2026-10-15T04:51:55Z

